&lt;p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'>&lt;span style='font-size:12.0pt'>            The
presentation here is not for &lt;u>solving&lt;/u> the creation-evolution problem, but
for &lt;u>clarifying&lt;/u> the issue and &lt;u>correcting&lt;/u> inappropriate thinking
patterns.&lt;/span>&lt;/p>
&lt;p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'>&lt;span style='font-size:12.0pt'>&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span>&lt;/p>
&lt;p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'>&lt;span style='font-size:12.0pt'>Identifying
the Issue&lt;/span>&lt;/p>
&lt;p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'>&lt;span style='font-size:12.0pt'>            Creationism
as such vs. the Christian formulations of it. There is a difference between
creation as a concept and the Judaeo-Christian—or even Islamic—formulation of
it. The Christian formulation gets into additional matters, which vary
according to the manner interpreters handle the relevant biblical materials.&lt;/span>&lt;/p></description></item><item><title>Natural Theology and New T estament</title><link>https://christir.org/essays/evidences/creation-and-evolution/natural-theology-and-new-t-estament/</link><pubDate>Thu, 02 Apr 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://christir.org/essays/evidences/creation-and-evolution/natural-theology-and-new-t-estament/</guid><description>&lt;style>
